{
	"name": "Marshlander",
	"type": "culture",
	"img": "icons/magic/nature/root-vine-thorned-fire-purple.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p><strong>Marshland Camouflage.</strong> You have mastered the ability to blend into the tangled reeds and logs. You gain proficiency in Stealth and an expertise die to checks made to camouflage yourself. If you spend 1 minute covering yourself in mud and leaves, you have advantage on checks made to Hide in wilderness areas. </p><p><strong>Muck Walker.</strong> You know how to tread through the mud and the muck. You are unaffected by difficult terrain caused by nonmagical swamps and marshes.</p><p><strong>Reed Weaver.</strong> Reeds and other grasses become a helpful tool in your hands. By spending 1 hour weaving grasses together, you may create a temporary shelter for you and your allies. This shelter repels rain and keeps Supply and up to 4 Medium or smaller creatures dry. This shelter lasts for 1 week, at which point it degrades and falls down.</p><p><strong>Languages.</strong> You may speak, read, write, and sign in Common and one other language of your choosing.</p>",
